An example in which 4-cores (1 thread each)  are simultaneously writing to
a shared array.

Use of the cpu-id (asr29) to differentiate the different cores in a 4-core processor.

Note that cpu-0 will setup the page tables.  Each cpu will
have a different initial stack pointer value.

To compile
./compile_for_ajit.sh

To run
ajit_C_system_model -n 4 -m mem_bw.mmap.remapped -w mem_bw.wtrace > serial.out 2> run.log
cat serial.out
